# vms-277 (SHOW CPU matches oracle): SHOW CPU layout on OpenVMS VAX V7.3.
# SHOW CPU output is deterministic here (static uniprocessor config), so the golden
# is reproducible as captured. The digit-mask 's/[0-9]/#/g' additionally masks the
# CPU numbers, node index and model number so the vms-c38 gate TOLERATES OVMX's
# own values (different CPU count / node / not a VAXserver) while still pinning the
# stable STRUCTURE: the multiprocessing-state line and the PRIMARY/Active/Configured
# CPU labels. (The node/model TEXT is machine-specific; the gate compares the
# labelled structure, not the model string.)
ARCH=vax
DESC="SHOW CPU layout — multiprocessing state + PRIMARY/Active/Configured CPU labels (numbers masked)"
NORMALIZE='s/[0-9]/#/g'
# MACHINE_MASK (vms-c38): the three SHOW CPU fields that legitimately vary by machine
# — masked so the gate compares the LABELLED STRUCTURE cross-system, not the values.
# Each s/// preserves the structural label and replaces only a NON-EMPTY value, so a
# blank/absent field still reds (guardrail: a mask means "this value varies", never
# "ignore this line"). Grounded, per src/vmsdcl/dcl_cmd_show.c (DCL-Dictionary-pinned,
# clean-room Rule 8) + the round-3 oracle diff:
#   1. the model-identity line — VAX "VAX1, a VAXserver 3900 Series" vs OVMX's own
#      "OVMX, an OVMX x86_64 system" (INV-1: OVMX keeps its real identity, never a
#      fabricated VMS model);
#   2. "Multiprocessing is ..." — ENABLED/DISABLED depends on the CPU count (a
#      machine fact), and VMS prints the "Uniprocessing synchronization image loaded"
#      clause only in the uniprocessor case (OVMX honestly omits it, INV-6);
#   3. "Active/Configured CPUs:" — a space-separated CPU-ID LIST whose length is the
#      CPU count (VAX uni = "01"; OVMX 2-way = "00 01"). DCL-Dictionary format.
# The labels (Multiprocessing is / PRIMARY CPU = / Active CPUs: / Configured CPUs:)
# are NOT masked and MUST match — that is the structure the gate pins.
MACHINE_MASK='s/^[A-Z0-9#]+, an? .* (Series|system)$/<CPU-MODEL>/; s/^(Multiprocessing is ).*/\1<MP-STATE>/; s/(Active CPUs: +)[#0-9 ]+$/\1<CPU-LIST>/; s/(Configured CPUs: +)[#0-9 ]+$/\1<CPU-LIST>/'
COMMANDS=(
  'SHOW CPU'
)
